        <h2 id="budget">How much should a small business spend on AI?</h2>
        <div class="chaprule"></div>
        <p>Less than the hype implies, and tied to revenue. SUCCESS suggests budgeting 1% to 3% of revenue for all technology, then putting 20% to 30% of that toward AI experiments (<a href="https://www.success.com/the-real-cost-of-ai-tools-for-small-business-roi-calculator-2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SUCCESS, 2026</a>). For a business with $500,000 in revenue, that is roughly $1,000 to $1,500 a year, enough to test two or three tools properly without overcommitting. Scale up only after a tool has proved its return. That discipline also keeps the stack small: a focused set of tools you actually use beats a drawer of subscriptions bought on impulse.</p>
        <div class="cta">
          <span class="kicker">Before your next renewal</span>
